<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Allahabad Pillar Inscription</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prayagraj">Allahabad</a> Pillar Inscription is a text inscribed on an earlier Ashokan pillar now at Allahabad (Prayagraj) in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It contains a eulogy of the Gupta emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samudragupta">Samudragupta</a> composed by the court poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harishena">Harishena</a>, listing his conquests and the rulers who submitted to him. It is a major source for the early history and expansion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a>.</p></div>
